\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{Why instruction data require serialization}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{instruction-tuning}

\p{The next-token law in \ref{ftip-000H} accepts token prefixes, whereas an
instruction dataset may store structured prompts. We formulate
\ref{ftip-006V} as the map between those types. Ouyang et al. describe SFT on
labeler demonstrations in \citet{Section 3.5 and Appendix C.1}{ouyang2022training};
their training account supplies a concrete pipeline rather than a universal
serializer.}

\p{A reproducible objective must retain the serializer revision with the
tokenizer and loss mask. Otherwise two runs can share an abstract dataset
name while optimizing different token sequences.}
